@startuml activity-handover
title Activity Diagram(Parcel Handover)
|Counter (Staff)|
start
:Resident presents the pickup code;
:Enter the pickup code;
|System|
if (Pickup code found?) then (no)
  |Counter (Staff)|
  :Verify identity: phone number and surname;\n(counter procedure: the contract has no fallback operation, CD-2);
  |System|
  if (Identity confirmed?) then (no)
    :Reject the handover;
    stop
  else (yes)
    :Record a manual handover for the operator;
    stop
  endif
else (yes)
  :Show the parcel and its location;
endif
if (Pickup code expired?) then (yes)
  :Reject the handover and tell the resident to ask for a new code;
  stop
endif
if (Pickup code already used?) then (yes)
  :Show the handover already recorded;\n(idempotent: 200, no second record);
  stop
endif
|Counter (Staff)|
:Fetch the parcel from the shelf;
:Confirm the handover;
|System|
fork
  :Mark the code used and record the handover;
fork again
  :Free the storage location;
end fork
note right
  Both branches are internal steps of the single
  POST /pickup/confirm transaction, not two endpoints.
end note
stop
@enduml
